course: dictionary
lesson: 14685
title: Presume: thinking something is likely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Presume means to think something is true without being sure, because it seems likely. «I presume the bus is late, because it is not here yet.» The speaker has not checked, but the clues make them think it is true.
explain: Presume can also mean treating something as true until it is proved wrong. In a court of law, a person is «presumed innocent» until it is proved otherwise. It can also mean being too bold: «Don't presume to tell me what to do» means you have no right to do that.
explain: To find the meaning, look at the words around presume. If someone says «I presume you've done your homework», they are guessing from clues, not knowing for certain. Try swapping in suppose or assume: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Presume means to think something is true without being sure, because it seems likely.
fact: «I presume you've done your homework» means the speaker thinks it is likely, but is not certain.
fact: «Presumed innocent» means treated as innocent until it is proved otherwise.
fact: «Presume on» or «presume upon» means to take unfair advantage of someone's kindness.
fact: The famous line «Dr Livingstone, I presume?» is a well-known example of presume used to guess who someone is.
exercise: «I presume the shop is closed, because the lights are off.» What does presume mean here? | Know for certain | Forget | Hope very much | *Think it is likely, without being sure
exercise: In a court, a person is «presumed innocent». What does this mean? | *Treated as innocent until it is proved otherwise | Sent home for the day | Given a prize for being honest | Known to be guilty already
exercise: «Don't presume to tell me what to do.» What does presume suggest? | Being very kind | Being sleepy | Being happy to help | *Being bold, with no right to do it
test: «He presumed his friend would come, so he kept a seat free.» What does presumed mean? | Forgot about it | Knew for certain | *Thought it likely, without being sure | Hoped it was not true
test: Which phrase means taking unfair advantage of someone's kindness? | Presumed dead | *Presume on their kindness | Presumed innocent | I presume
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to presume in «I presume you are tired»? | Hope | Forget | *Suppose | Shout
